WEBVTT

00:04:28.528 --> 00:04:31.568
DC: It was, weirdly,
the only job that I could get.

00:04:31.871 --> 00:04:35.402
AG: Dave turned out to be
unusually humble and hardworking.

00:04:35.426 --> 00:04:37.119
He was a diamond in the rough.

00:04:37.946 --> 00:04:39.413
So now when he hires,

00:04:39.437 --> 00:04:41.059
he's determined to give candidates

00:04:41.083 --> 00:04:43.138
who might not make
a great first impression,

00:04:43.162 --> 00:04:44.377
a second chance.

00:04:44.401 --> 00:04:50.094
DC: I'll take hungry and eager
over supertalented,

00:04:50.118 --> 00:04:52.174
really any day of the week.

00:04:52.198 --> 00:04:54.279
AG: But before you hire someone,

00:04:54.303 --> 00:04:56.964
it can be tough to get
an accurate read on their talent,

00:04:56.988 --> 00:04:58.440
let alone their character.

00:04:58.464 --> 00:05:01.566
DC: The interview process,
as a whole, is pretty stupid.